<<~ ahu slot=`#/head`>>

! engine.home.reads ~ the the operator's homes tunnel read: every item's state, nothing written

`lares home read` reads every operator home the device carries (seats, hooks, the seed rule) against its declaration and the ledger of what the house last wrote, and writes nothing. Each row names its state (aligned, drift, foreign, unreachable, absent), its id, its path and whether a hand touched it since the house wrote it; the exit class carries the worst state. `--brief` prints the one line the wake hook reads, with or without a terminal. The home door keeps no checkout and reads no index: `--root` and `--staged` refuse with exit 2 and name the repo door.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/shows`>>

!! shows ~ read · brief

```memetic-wikitext
<<has entity=`example` name=`read` params=`~ read the operator's homes's tunnel`>>
<<has entity=`example` name=`brief` params=`brief/true ~ the one line a hook reads`>>
```

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/takes`>>

!! takes ~ familiar · brief · root · staged

```memetic-wikitext
<<has entity=`arg` name=`familiar` params=`takes/pet-name ~ the familiar whose hooks a home tend seats; absent, the one already seated stands`>>
<<has entity=`arg` name=`brief` params=`~ print the one line a hook reads, terminal or none`>>
<<has entity=`arg` name=`root` params=`takes/dir ~ refused here: only lares repo keeps a checkout`>>
<<has entity=`arg` name=`staged` params=`~ refused here: only lares repo read reads the index`>>
```

<<~/ahu>>

